	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7321"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 59<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=788.msg7321#msg7321"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=788.msg7321#msg7321">Re:Laterz</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #34 on:</b> April 27, 2004, 05:13:59 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Delheru, do you realize that since last August. &nbsp;We&#039;ve only lost 3...maybe 4 people to Ascent?</div><br />It&#039;s amazing you lost any at all between LDoN coming out and the last month or so, since we never had our applications open. Ascent played one day every week for like 6 months after all, and before the unfinished nature of some of GoDs content started rubbing in, we had no need to recruit to fill up the smaller raids in GoD (which were - how typical is this - bugged to a smaller size than they were meant to be).<br /><br />Now that we have apps open there&#039;s apps from pretty much everyone around except DA/EiE. That actually confuses me some, since DA/EiE actually has way too many people still, and just last sunday I saw their people waiting outside their PoTime raid in PoTA (since they had 72 people in PoTB). On the other hand we killed Quarm on sunday as well simply to get away from GoD, and we had 44 people there. Guess it&#039;s just a different type of guild, and their members feel they would not enjoy the way Ascent plays the game. The irony is in the fact that a lot of DA/EiE members (I should say, officers) are most &quot;Ascentline&quot; than most Ascent members &gt;&lt;<br /><br /><br /><br />Anyway I&#039;d never deny Eelyens significance to the server as a figure. Considering the timespans involved, I&#039;d probably considering him as the most significant non-Ascent player in the history of RN. Jeet would probably be it, except DA/EiE always kept more to themselves, and because of that tended to get less people involved in their activities. Poor Axine is being diminished by time =(
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
